            ],
            "data": {
                "text": "## 1. Reads, quality control and host removal\n\nGive the paired-end short reads and, if available, the long reads (then set *Long reads provided?* to Yes). Short reads are trimmed with fastp and depleted of host/contaminant reads with Bowtie2. The long-read branch trims and filters the nanopore reads, removes contaminants with Kraken2 and depletes host reads with minimap2. When no long reads are given, one empty FASTA per sample stands in, so the assembly step always receives a sample-matched collection."
            }
        },
