                    "input_subworkflow_step_id": 4
                }
            },
            "inputs": [],
            "outputs": [],
            "annotation": "Embedded workflow: trims adapters and low-quality bases with fastp and summarises read quality with MultiQC.",
            "when": null,
            "id": 101,
            "uuid": "d4750314-8ac8-4dd9-897b-e28da8534f59",
            "position": {
                "left": 760,
                "top": 365
            },
            "workflow_outputs": [
                {
                    "label": "Trimmed short reads",
                    "output_name": "fastp trimmed reads",
                    "uuid": "b71be1cc-9ece-4fb8-91e1-a01ffaeaf9e3"
                },
                {
                    "label": "Short-read QC report",
                    "output_name": "MultiQC HTML report",
                    "uuid": "458e72b5-a938-41a0-a654-9179d2cd7096"
                }
            ],
            "subworkflow": {
                "a_galaxy_workflow": "true",
                "annotation": "This workflow performs quality control and trimming on paired-end Illumina fastq(.gz) files using fastp and aggregates the quality control reports with MultiQC",
                "comments": [],
                "creator": [
                    {
                        "class": "Person",
                        "identifier": "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9852-1987",
                        "name": "Bérénice Batut"
                    },
                    {
                        "class": "Person",
                        "identifier": "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2982-388X",
                        "name": "Paul Zierep"
                    },
                    {
                        "class": "Person",
                        "identifier": "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-3602-7884",
                        "name": "Mina Hojat Ansari"
                    },
                    {
                        "class": "Organization",
                        "name": "FAIRyMAGs consortium",
                        "url": "https://github.com/usegalaxy-eu/FAIRyMAGs"
                    }
                ],
                "format-version": "0.1",
                "license": "MIT",
                "name": "Short-read quality control and trimming",
                "readme": "# Short-read quality control and trimming\n\nBefore starting any analysis, it is always a good idea to assess the quality of the input data and to discard poor-quality base content by trimming and filtering reads.\n\nThis workflow can be used on its own or integrated into other workflows. For example, it is part of a **suite of workflows for end-to-end metagenome-assembled genome (MAG) generation** (check [FAIRyMAGs repository](https://github.com/usegalaxy-eu/FAIRyMAGs) for the complete workflow suite and its capabilities).\nA dedicated [learning pathway](https://galaxyproject.github.io/training-material/learning-pathways/mags.html) provides detailed guidance on how to use this workflow.\n\nThis workflow takes paired-end Illumina (**short-reads**) fastq(.gz) files and executes the following steps:\n1. Quality control and trimming using **fastp**\n2. Aggregation of the quality control reports using **MultiQC**\n\n## Input Datasets\n\n- A list of paired datasets corresponding to paired-end raw reads in `fastqsanger` or `fastqsanger.gz` format.\n- Qualified quality score: The quality value that a base is qualified to have.\n- Minimal read length: Reads shorter than this value will be discarded.\n- [Optional] Adapter to remove on forward reads and reverse reads\n\n## Output Datasets\n\n- A list of paired datasets corresponding to paired-end **trimmed** reads in `fastqsanger` or `fastqsanger.gz`, ready for further analysis.\n- List of `JSON` reports of fastp for each sample that could be used as inputs for extra MultiQC\n- MultiQC report in HTML\n\n## Funding\n\nThis workflow was developed as part of the [**FAIRyMAGs** project](https://elixir-europe.org/how-we-work/scientific-programme/science/bfsp/fairymags), funded as a commissioned service of the [**Biodiversity, Food Security and Pathogens (BFSP) ELIXIR Scientific Programme 2024–2028**](https://elixir-europe.org/how-we-work/scientific-programme/science/bfsp).\n\nThe project was also supported by the **European Galaxy Server**, funded by the German Federal Ministry of Education and Research (BMBF; 031 A538A de.NBI-RBC) and the **Ministry of Science, Research and the Arts Baden-Württemberg (MWK)** within the framework of **LIBIS/de.NBI Freiburg**.",
                "report": {
                    "markdown": "\n# Workflow Execution Report\n\n## Workflow Inputs\n```galaxy\ninvocation_inputs()\n```\n\n## Workflow Outputs\n```galaxy\ninvocation_outputs()\n```\n\n## Workflow\n```galaxy\nworkflow_display()\n```\n"
                },
                "steps": {
