                                "1": {
                                    "annotation": "Paired-end reads of each sample (list:paired), quality-trimmed and host-removed. Each sample's reads are mapped against every assembly. Multi-sample binning is most effective with up to ~20 samples (performance peaks around 20; Mineeva et al., Nat. Commun. 2025, https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-026-71521-w). Using more than 20 samples can lead to extensive resource usage (N² mappings, large storage). For more than 20 samples or unrelated environments, single-sample binning may be cheaper.",
